.TH V32C++\-HEADERS 3v32 "October 20, 2026" "v32c++ 20261020-release" "v32c++ Library"
.SH NAME
v32c++\-headers \- the C++ headers and the C library that come with v32c++
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
C++ input:
.PP
.B #include <v32/video.hpp>
.B #include <v32/input.hpp>
.B #include <v32/audio.hpp>
.B #include <v32/time.hpp>
.B #include <v32/math.hpp>
.B #include <v32/string.hpp>
.B #include <v32/misc.hpp>
.B #include <v32/memcard.hpp>
.B #include <v32/keyboard.hpp>
.B #include <v32/mouse.hpp>
.B #include <v32/v32io.hpp>
.PP
.B #include <string>
.B #include <array>
.B #include <vector>
.B #include <cstdarg>
.PP
C input:
.PP
.B #include <stdio.h>
.RB "(and " stdlib.h ", " ctype.h ", " unistd.h ", " curses.h ", ...)"
.B #include <v32libc.c>
.B #include <v32curses.c>
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR v32c++ (1)
translates C++ (or, for a
.I .c
file, C) into the C dialect of the Vircon32 console, compiled by
.BR compile (1).
Three groups of headers come with it.
.SS The v32 headers
.I v32/*.hpp
is a C++ layer over the Vircon32 SDK headers described in
.BR vircon32 (3v32).
Each one includes its SDK header (the
.B #include
line passes through to the generated C) and adds, in namespace
.BR v32 ,
what C cannot express: typed enums for the SDK's
.BR #define s,
overload sets, scope-guard classes that restore the console's
\(lqselected\(rq texture, gamepad, sound or channel when they go out of
scope, and small handle classes. Nothing in them touches the hardware
directly; every port access is a call into the SDK.
.PP
.TS
l l.
\fBvideo.hpp\fR(3v32)	BlendMode, TextureScope, Point, draw helpers
\fBinput.hpp\fR(3v32)	bool readers, Button, GamepadScope
\fBaudio.hpp\fR(3v32)	Channel, SoundScope, ChannelScope
\fBtime.hpp\fR(3v32)	Date, TimeOfDay, Stopwatch, FrameScope
\fBmath.hpp\fR(3v32)	minimum, maximum, absolute, clamp, lerp, ...
\fBstring.hpp\fR(3v32)	String, a fixed-capacity string class
\fBmisc.hpp\fR(3v32)	random ranges, word helpers, HeapBlock
\fBmemcard.hpp\fR(3v32)	MemoryCard, a signature-checked save slot
.TE
.PP
Three more give programs a keyboard and a mouse through the v32io
protocol, which needs either the v32io hardware adaptor or a modified
emulator:
.PP
.TS
l l.
\fBv32io.hpp\fR(3v32)	IoDevice, the common core
\fBkeyboard.hpp\fR(3v32)	Keyboard, with typed characters (accents, box drawing)
\fBmouse.hpp\fR(3v32)	Mouse
.TE
.SS Built-in standard headers
.BR <string> ,
.B <array>
and
.B <vector>
have no files: the transpiler provides
.BR std::string ,
.B std::array
and
.B std::vector
itself (see
.BR v32c++\-string (3v32),
.BR v32c++\-array (3v32)
and
.BR v32c++\-vector (3v32)).
.B <cstdarg>
(or
.BR <stdarg.h> )
provides
.B va_list
and the
.B va_
macros for variadic functions.
.SS The C library
For C input,
.I libc/
holds the part of the standard C library that ordinary C programs
expect, plus curses, written for the console in C and transpiled with
the program. Its standard-named headers
.RB ( stdio.h ", " stdlib.h ", " ctype.h ", " errno.h ", " limits.h ,
.BR memory.h ", " signal.h ", " stddef.h ", " unistd.h ", " fcntl.h ,
.BR sys/types.h ", " sys/stat.h )
all include one declarations header,
.IR v32libc.h ,
and the code is brought in by
including
.I v32libc.c
(and
.I v32curses.c
for curses) once, since Vircon32 programs are a single translation
unit.
.PP
.TS
l l.
\fBv32libc\fR(3v32)	stdio, stdlib, string, ctype, errno, signal, time
\fBv32file\fR(3v32)	files on the memory card
\fBv32term\fR(3v32)	80\(mu24 text screen, gamepad, on-screen keyboard
\fBv32curses\fR(3v32)	curses
.TE
.SH SEARCH PATH
An
.B #include
of a
.I .hpp
or
.I .cpp
file, and in C input of any
.I .h
or
.I .c
file other than the eight SDK header names, is resolved and read by
.B v32c++
itself. The quoted form looks in the including file's directory, each
.B \-I
directory, the current directory, each directory of
.BR $V32CXX_INCLUDE ,
and the installed header directory, in that order; the angle-bracket
form skips the first and third. The installed directory is
.I /usr/local/Vircon32/v32tools/include/v32c++
by default (it holds
.I v32/
and
.IR libc/ ,
so
.B #include <v32/video.hpp>
works from anywhere), and C input also searches its
.I libc/
subdirectory.
.PP
An SDK header
.RB ( video.h ", " input.h ", " audio.h ", " time.h ", " math.h ,
.BR string.h ", " misc.h ", " memcard.h )
is not expanded, in C input as in C++, so
.B #include <string.h>
and
.B #include <time.h>
in a C program reach the SDK's headers, not the C library's: its
.B #include
line passes through to the generated C, where
.BR compile (1)
finds it. When
.B v32c++
can find the header too \(em on the search path, in
.BR $V32CXX_SDK_INCLUDE ,
next to a
.B compile
on
.BR $PATH ,
or in
.I /usr/local/Vircon32/DevTools/include
\(em it reads it, so that its macros and its struct and typedef names
can be used from C++.
.SH CONVENTIONS
.IP \(bu 2
A wrapper never has the same name as the SDK function it wraps
.RB ( v32::minimum ,
not
.BR v32::min ),
so the SDK's C functions stay available unchanged and an unqualified
call inside the namespace cannot find the wrapper instead.
.IP \(bu 2
Every parameter and return value is one word, as Vircon32 C requires:
results that need more come back through a pointer argument
.RB ( v32::screen_center(Point*) ),
and classes are passed by pointer or reference.
.IP \(bu 2
Scope guards and handle classes are meant to be local variables; their
destructors run at the end of the block, on every path out of it.
There are no exceptions.
.IP \(bu 2
As in the SDK, sizes are in 32-bit words and a character is a word.
.IP \(bu 2
A function in a namespace is emitted under a C name that includes the
namespace and parameter types
.RI ( v32::draw(int,int,int)
becomes
.IR v32__draw__int_int_int );
a class keeps its bare name in the C.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/local/Vircon32/v32tools/include/v32c++/v32/
The v32 headers.
.TP
.I /usr/local/Vircon32/v32tools/include/v32c++/libc/
The C library.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B V32CXX_INCLUDE
Colon-separated directories searched before the installed header
directory.
.TP
.B V32CXX_SDK_INCLUDE
Colon-separated directories searched for the SDK's
.I .h
headers.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR v32c++ (1),
.BR vircon32 (3v32),
.BR compile (1)
.PP
In the source distribution:
.IR docs/V32IO.md ,
.IR docs/C_INPUT.md ,
.IR docs/STRING.md ,
.IR docs/GENERICS.md ,
.IR docs/NATIVE_PASSTHROUGH.md .
.SH AUTHOR
Matthew Haas
